  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is the semi-minor axis of an ellipse,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are its focii and the angle between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a right angle, then the square of the eccentricity of the ellipse is",
    "image": null
